 "refs": [
  {
   "title": "How to tell time",
   "html": "<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table class=\"ref\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">È l'una</td><td>1:00. Singular, so È. Same for È mezzogiorno, È mezzanotte.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">Sono le + hour</td><td>Sono le tre. Every other hour is plural.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">… e + minutes</td><td>Sono le tre e dieci (3:10)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">… e un quarto</td><td>Sono le tre e un quarto (3:15)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">… e mezzo / mezza</td><td>Sono le tre e mezzo (3:30)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">next hour meno …</td><td>Sono le quattro meno un quarto (3:45), meno dieci (3:50)</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">24-hour clock</td><td>Sono le quindici e quarantacinque (15:45). Used for trains, shops, appointments.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">part of day</td><td>di mattina · del pomeriggio · di sera · di notte</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table></div>\n    <h3 class=\"refh\">Asking and answering</h3>\n    <p class=\"reftip\"><b>Che ore sono?</b> → Sono le… (what time is it now)<br><b>A che ora…?</b> → Alle… / All'una / A mezzogiorno (at what time does something happen)</p>"
  },
  {
   "title": "Which little word with dates and times?",
   "html": "<div class=\"tblwrap\"><table class=\"ref\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Use</th><th>Before</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">a / ad</td><td>months, holidays</td><td>a giugno · ad agosto · a Pasqua</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">il</td><td>a date</td><td>il quattro luglio · il primo maggio</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">alle / all'</td><td>clock times</td><td>alle nove · all'una</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">a</td><td>noon, midnight</td><td>a mezzogiorno · a mezzanotte</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">il / la + day</td><td>every week</td><td>il martedì · la domenica</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">di + day</td><td>recurring day</td><td>di giovedì</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">day alone</td><td>one specific day</td><td>Arrivo martedì.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">nel</td><td>years, centuries, weekend</td><td>nel 2026 · nel Novecento</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">al</td><td>ordinals (floors…)</td><td>al terzo piano</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">dalle … alle</td><td>from … to (times)</td><td>dalle nove alle cinque</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">tra / fra</td><td>in (from now)</td><td>tra un'ora</td></tr>\n        <tr><td class=\"k\">… fa</td><td>ago</td><td>tre giorni fa</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table></div>"
  },
  {
   "title": "Notes on the handouts",
   "html": "<ul class=\"fixes\">\n      <li><b>Compagna</b> (Handout 4.2) should be <b>campagna</b>, countryside. Compagna means a female companion.</li>\n      <li>In the dialogue, <b>“Li trova tutti gli orari”</b> should be <b>Lì trova</b> (there you'll find). Li without the accent means “them”. Likewise <b>“Si, ed è gratis”</b> should be <b>Sì</b> (yes).</li>\n      <li>The handout's <b>Vai dritto</b> is the tu form. To a stranger, use Lei: <b>Vada dritto, giri a destra, attraversi la strada, prenda la prima a sinistra</b>.</li>\n      <li>The 1st of the month is <b>il primo</b> (il primo maggio). Every other date uses a plain number.</li>\n      <li>Real-life note: you stamp (timbrare) paper tickets for <b>regional</b> trains. Frecciarossa tickets have a reserved seat and don't need stamping.</li>\n    </ul>"
  }
 ]
}